kind how-do-i
title How do I turn on the live trial when the console has allow-font-ops off?
intro The live trial switches the console's font for a few seconds with OSC 50, which a vtium console answers only while allow-font-ops is on. vtium reads allow-font-ops when it starts, and vtium-config asks the console once, when vtium-config starts. So the trial works only after you install the change, restart vtium, and start vtium-config again.
see fonts/try-a-font-set-whose-font-is-not-active

# The console started with allow-font-ops off.
file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = mono
    no-allow-font-ops
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
    ROOT/fonts/wide.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
font fonts/wide.bdf 10x20
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
frit wide
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/wide.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
at the Looks tab
check screen shows "this vtium console has allow-font-ops turned off"
check screen shows "install, and restart vtium and vtium-config."
2. Highlight wide.
3. Press t.
at t
check console never-received "\e]50;wide"
check console draws mono

4. Go to the Settings tab.
5. Choose Fonts and text.
6. Highlight allow-font-ops.
7. Press Enter.
8. Highlight on.
9. Press Enter.
10. Press Esc.
11. Press s to save.
12. Press i to install.
13. Press y for yes.
at the install
check installed lacks "no-allow-font-ops"
14. Press q to quit.
15. Restart vtium.
note vtium now answers OSC 50. Start vtium-config again, and t tries a font set on the console.
